      "words": 49
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "My jeans and white T-shirt are fine for walking around town or sitting by the lake. But this is the fanciest restaurant ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8989
        },
        {
          "text": "“You’re not paying,” he says. “It’s my treat.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 9297
        },
        {
          "text": "“Fine,” I relent. I’ll order the cheapest thing on the menu. Breadsticks. A side salad. “But only if you actually pay.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11400
        }
      ],
      "words": 55
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Nothing, really,” he admits. “The Agency provides inane activities under the guise of building morale. We have broken p",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 16524
        },
        {
          "text": "Daniel is quiet for so long that I begin to wonder if he’s going to ignore the question. Perhaps I’ve overstepped",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17204
        },
        {
          "text": "“I haven’t been able to stand it,” he admits. “Not until you.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17529
        }
      ],
      "words": 65
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I grab a blue stick of it and draw an exaggerated stick figure on the ground, leaning into the camp of it all",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 20354
        },
        {
          "text": "I wanted to be a graphic novelist when I was a kid",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 21556
        },
        {
